-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 17 13:18:21 UTC 2026 - malcolmlewis@opensuse.org

- Updated to version 8.38.0:
  * Add preview of VPP filters, (With additionally included
    HWEncVppPreview).
  * Add --seek support for avi/avs/vpy input.
  * Improve --vpp-colorspace VUI output.
  * Fix error when multiple --vpp-colorspace filters are chained.
  * Fix --vpp-colorspace failing with no path when range and matrix
    (or similar) change in the same stage.
  * --vpp-afs and --vpp-kfm mode=24 count output timestamps from
    the first input frame.
  * Fix --vpp-afs timestamp drift with --avsync vfr and a custom
    --timebase.
  * Fix GPU counter thread shutdown.
- Changes from version 8.37.0:
  * Fix hw decode error on Sandy Bridge (and probably Ivy Bridge)
    when using --adapt-resolution.
- Changes from version 8.36.0:
  * Fix old frames mixed in when using --vpp-kfm.
  * Speed up --vpp-kfm.
  * Run single-frame, multi-frame, and mask pre/post processing of
    --vpp-onnx on the OpenCL path.
  * Add --vpp-vhs-restore. (rigaya/HWEnc-onnx-models#1).
- Changes from version 8.35.0:
  * Speed up reconstruction in --vpp-kfm and --vpp-rtgmc.
  * Speed up --vpp-kfm when ucf=on.
  * Reduce memory use of --vpp-kfm and --vpp-rtgmc.
  * Reduce CPU usage of --opencl-task-threads 2.
  * Fix encode failure on Linux when the iHD driver is in a
    non-standard location and QSV cannot be used.
  * Fix encode failure when --avhw is specified with VA-API
    selected.
  * Fix abnormal exit on interrupt.
  * Fix --vpp-kfm mode=24,ucf=on stopping output.
  * Fix --vpp-kfm ucf=on exiting with an error at the end of
    VFR/P24 output.
  * Fix --vpp-kfm 24p, UCF, and high bit-depth output stopping.
- Changes from version 8.34.0:
  * Improve stability when the encoder is busy.
- Changes from version 8.33.0:
  * Wait 1 ms on encoder busy retry to reduce CPU utilization,
    (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#334).
  * Improve --seek and --seekto accuracy on mpegts/mp4 input,
    (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#326 and gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#328).
  * Improve --trim behavior on short mpegts videos,
    (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#330).
  * Sync the VPP output before --ssim, --psnr, or --vmaf reads it,
    fixing failures and wrong scores, (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#319).
  * Fix --ssim over 1.0 when the plane size is not a multiple of 4,
    (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#322).
  * Stop the encode with an error instead of dropping frames and
    exiting successfully when a task fails during pipeline flush,
    (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#320).
  * Continue OpenCL processing on a VA decode-error report so
    trailing frames are not lost, (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#333).
  * Fix cases where the encoder waited 5 seconds before exiting,
    (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#332).
  * Fix error log output on Linux when IO statistics are
    unavailable, (gh#rigaya/QNVEnc#807).
  * Fix --vpp-kfm output information to progressive, and inherit
    SAR for raw output.
  * Speed up block analysis in --vpp-kfm.
  * Speed up the detail-reference blur in --vpp-rtgmc-retouch.
- Changes from version 8.32.0:
  * Add VA-API encoding support on Linux. (--backend)
  * Disable --la-depth in ICQ mode. ICQ with LookaheadDepth can
    stall before encode starts on some Intel graphics drivers,
    (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#315).
  * Synchronize MFX VPP output before encode on Linux VA memory,
    fixing old frames mixed in by color conversion and same-format
    resize, (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#308).
  * Improve CPU utilization information on Linux systems.
  * Fix TrueHD audio timestamp calculation,
    (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#805).
  * Optimize --vpp-rtgmc search-prefilter. Exclude the repair path
    from the program when it is unused (about 8x), and inline it
    for profiles with small expansion.
  * Reduce host sync waits in --vpp-kfm so GPU submission stays
    continuous.
  * Optimize motion search in --vpp-degrain.
  * Reduce --vpp-nnedi output initialization to the kept field on
    processed planes.
  * Use the subgroup predictor in --vpp-nnedi even when the
    auto-selected SIMD width is not 16 or 32.
  * Deepen the encoder output queue so encode waits overlap filter
    processing.
  * Fix missing completion events for interlaced --vpp-resize and
    fix --vpp-rtgmc-search-prefilter search_refine=3 producing 0
    frames.
  * Fix crash when using OpenCL vpp filters with --output-csp
    yuv444, (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#311).
- Changes from version 8.31.0:
  * Fix OpenCL interop failure when multiple Intel OpenCL platforms
    are present.
  * Fix device-not-found platform search results being reported as
    errors when multiple Intel OpenCL platforms are present.
  * Fix --vpp-afs failure on environments without
    cl_khr_image2d_from_buffer.
  * Fix --vpp-afs non deterministic behaviour.
  * Fix a crash on exit in --vpp-afs with YUV444.
  * Fix pixel format conversion.
  * Fix --frames used together with --trim referring to the empty
    trim list just after initialization.
  * Fix an out-of-bounds write at the end of a row in --vpp-tweak,
    (gh#rigaya/QSVEnc#313).
- Add 341.patch: Fix build and loading with libplacebo API 387.
  FIXME: Declined upstream since QSVEnc does not support the
  --vpp-libplacebo-* filters on Linux. Disable libplacebo build
  option, see <https://github.com/rigaya/QSVEnc/pull/341>.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Sep 16 20:35:40 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 8.30+0:
  * Add --vmaf to calculate VMAF of the encoded video
  * Add --vpp-kfm inverse telecine, --vpp-rtgmc deinterlace and
    --vpp-degrain
  * Add further VPP filters (bm3d, dehaze, clahe, lenscorrection
    and others)
  * Support track exclusion with ! for audio/subtitle/data
    selection
  * Follow mid-stream input resolution changes
    (--adapt-resolution)
  * Default --avsync to vfr to reduce audio desync on TS drops
  * Multi-thread OpenCL pipeline on Ice Lake and later
  * Improve Linux support with the Intel Xe kernel driver
  * Fix OpenCL artifacts with --avhw, y4m timestamps and P010
    10-bit output
  * Many more filters, fixes and performance work; see upstream's
    release notes for the full list
- Switch the Linux build from configure to meson
- Pass -Wl,-z,noexecstack (replaces the old configure extra-ldflags)
- Drop QSVEnc-remove-git.patch and QSVEnc-enable-vulkan.patch
- Add QSVEnc-system-libs.patch: use system libvpl, skip bundled
  libhdr10plus-rs, and accept Factory VapourSynth V4-only headers
- Enable Vulkan, libplacebo and VMAF via meson options
- Convert obs_scm and set_version service modes from disabled to
  manual

-------------------------------------------------------------------
